  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What feeds the task list",
      "items": [
        "Five platforms are read through connectors: Windows Task Scheduler (through the local agent), Claude Code routines, Gemini Triggers, GitHub Actions and n8n. Vercel Cron, also read-only, follows the same connector-to-sync path and is left off the map to keep it readable. Quick links are navigation only and feed nothing.",
        "Periodic sync is on by default: each connection refreshes its tracked tasks every 30 minutes (5 minutes to a day, or off). It is refresh-only, so it never adopts a new folder or clears an exclusion; Import and Refresh run the same sync on demand.",
        "The native scheduler checks due jobs every 30 seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Reading and controlling are different paths",
      "items": [
        "Primary arrows show data returned by source reads. Reverse arrows show representative Run commands dispatched by Cronsole.",
        "Windows: the agent reads Task Scheduler, sends snapshots over Socket.IO, and verifies signed commands before starting a task.",
        "Claude: session OAuth reads and controls hosted routines. Without it, declared entries and per-routine fire tokens are the fallback; a declared entry is not a live platform read. A start acknowledgement does not prove completion."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Platform boundaries",
      "items": [
        "GitHub Actions is an observer: reads scheduled workflows, YAML schedules and run outcomes, from named repositories and from watched owners (re-expanded each sync, skipping forks, archived repositories and GitHub-managed workflows); changes and runs stay on GitHub.",
        "n8n reads workflows and execution results through REST. Run requires an MCP token; publishing and editing stay in n8n.",
        "Gemini supports run, create, pause and delete. In-place schedule/prompt changes are unavailable; recreation is a separate operation. Claude deletion stays in claude.ai."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One app view; different execution owners",
      "items": [
        "Scope + sync filters tracked folders or configured scope and exclusions, then upserts platform tasks without overwriting user labels, except that GitHub, n8n, Gemini and OAuth-read Claude names follow the platform (Cronsole cannot rename them there). Partial listings must not retire missing tasks.",
        "Native job definitions already live in PostgreSQL: no external import or Windows agent. The backend executes HTTP, program, script and check jobs and stores their outcomes. Due runs more than five minutes late are skipped.",
        "The dashboard reads stored task data through REST. Socket.IO task:updated invalidates queries and prompts a refetch; PostgreSQL does not push directly to the browser.",
        "Platform run history/output is read separately on demand where supported; it is not all copied into ExecutionLog."
      ]
    }
  ]
